      "body": "A lifecycle test could repeatedly open an SSE subscription, close the client side without sending another event, and assert that the server-side connection and file-descriptor count return to baseline within a timeout. Including both an idle stream and one closed immediately after receiving an event would cover the likely cleanup paths. This would guard against fixes that detect disconnects only during the next write.\n",
